      "writtenOn": "2024-02-05T15:52:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does crosvm give us the guarantee that the \"OPP topology\" is 1-to-1 between tables and vCPUs?\n\n\nFor example, with real hardware (or vCPU-to-CPU pinning), a DT could describe multiple clusters where all CPUs within a cluster share the same properties (including OPPs) e.g.\n```\ncpus {\n    cpu@0 { operating-points-v2 \u003d \u003c\u0026opp_table_little\u003e; };\n    cpu@1 { operating-points-v2 \u003d \u003c\u0026opp_table_little\u003e; };\n    cpu@2 { operating-points-v2 \u003d \u003c\u0026opp_table_mid\u003e; };\n    cpu@3 { operating-points-v2 \u003d \u003c\u0026opp_table_mid\u003e; };\n    cpu@4 { operating-points-v2 \u003d \u003c\u0026opp_table_big\u003e; };\n    cpu@5 { operating-points-v2 \u003d \u003c\u0026opp_table_big\u003e; };\n\n    opp_table_little: opp-table-little { ... };\n    opp_table_mid: opp-table-mid { ... };\n    opp_table_big: opp-table-big { ... };\n}\n```\nbut the code in this CL seems to assume that such a topology wouldn\u0027t be received, is this correct?\n\nOOC, how does vCPU cpufreq handle vCPU thread migration between physical CPUs?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 60,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 60,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "5306457eca6defbbadab16c726424d6ac4a7918a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e9f2da40_47a224cb",
        "filename": "pvmfw/platform.dts",
