      "writtenOn": "2024-02-06T04:38:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, these properties are optional and should not prevent boot. I think putting it inside of the cpu nodes makes a lot of sense, at least from a patching DT point of view. But how \"true to life\" do these nodes have to be? I.E. I don\u0027t think you\u0027d want to include opp entries inside of CPU nodes purely for readability reasons. But since crosvm is the one generating these nodes, it doesn\u0027t really matter how readable it is.\n\nActually is your comment applying to the DT being fed in or the DT that\u0027s being patched/generated. Does the layout of the DT between being fed in have to match the generated layout?",
      "parentUuid": "28b3aa06_18c984b2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 169,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 169,
        "endChar": 26
      },
