      "writtenOn": "2024-02-06T21:53:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Does the layout of the DT between being fed in have to match the generated layout?\n\nYes, ideally the impact of pvmfw should not be observable by the guest.\n\nOf course, pvmfw doesn\u0027t currently actually follow that rule (e.g. properties being stripped if not expected) but nodes moving around the DT (i.e. being at different paths) might be a bit of a stretch.\n\nSo my comment was about both the crosvm-generated input DT and (by symmetry) the one being patched by pvmfw; do you think that\u0027d be possible? The Linux docs don\u0027t seem to mandate a path (although the examples do suggest putting them at the root).\n\nBTW, if pvmfw\u0027s `read_*()` function locates the nodes by `\u003ccompatible\u003e` (or by following the phandle, which might make more sense IMO), it won\u0027t actually matter to it where the table nodes are located within the input DT, meaning that crosvm could be patched to place them at another path without breaking pvmfw.",
      "parentUuid": "edb1aaae_32dd6682",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 169,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 169,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "5306457eca6defbbadab16c726424d6ac4a7918a",
